  "report": {
    "incident_title": "API gateway p99 latency and 504s spiking",
    "outcome": "conclusive",
    "summary": "Gateway 5xx and high p99 latency were triggered by downstream delays, not by gateway load. At 18:30 a feature-flag rollout increased the size of catalog product-page cache entries (now including reviews). 45 min later Redis hit 100 % of its 8 GB limit, evicting hot keys (>5 k/s) and cutting the hit-ratio from 95 % to 40 %. Cache misses forced catalog-svc to fetch reviews from Postgres; DB CPU pegged at ~99 % and individual review queries took ~4.6 s. Catalog-svc\u2019s p99 therefore rose to the API-gateway timeout (5 s) and the gateway reported 504s. Gateway CPU stayed low, so scaling it would not have helped.\n\nRoot cause: Growth team\u2019s \u201cpdp_cache_include_reviews\u201d feature flag rollout increased cached value size, exhausting Redis and cascading latency to the database and gateway.",
    "root_cause": "Feature flag pdp_cache_include_reviews increased cache value size, causing Redis memory exhaustion, evictions, low hit-ratio, DB overload and gateway timeouts.",
